# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT THESE. This is the file standing between a public repo and a
# private Airtable base. Do not remove lines from it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your own scanner patterns — your employer, medication, biometrics, etc.
# NEVER COMMIT. The .example file is the public, placeholder-only version.
tools/private-patterns.txt
**/private-patterns.txt
!tools/private-patterns.example.txt

# The vocabulary rename map. A published "condition X -> word Y" list is a
# decoder ring that undoes the neutralisation. NEVER COMMIT.
tools/private-renames.json
**/private-renames.json
!tools/private-renames.example.json

# Local configuration — base ID, field IDs, personal targets, coach prompt.
app/config.js
config.js
**/config.local.js

# The private, un-sanitised build. Keep it outside the repo if you can;
# this is the belt-and-braces in case you don't.
private/
*.private.html
index.private.html
abhinavos-deploy.zip
*-deploy.zip

# Data exports of any kind.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.json.bak
export/
exports/
backup/
backups/
apple-health-export*
*.gpx

# Personal imagery. Your own avatar/logo files stay local unless you
# deliberately commit them to YOUR fork (which is fine — they're yours).
# NOTE: app/assets/framework-mark-*.png ARE tracked — they are the framework
# attribution mark, not personal branding. Your own images go elsewhere:
app/assets/my-*
app/assets/avatar*
avatar.*
boot.*
face.*
progress-photos/

# Secrets by convention.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets*
credentials*

# OS and editor noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# AI assistant working directories. The documented way to build your own
# version is to open this repository with an AI coding assistant and paste
# your details into it. These folders accumulate session transcripts and
# scratch files that can contain a pasted token or a filled-in config.
.claude/
.cursor/
.continue/
.aider*

# Archives. A zipped copy of a working install contains your config.js.
*.zip

# Logs.
*.log

# Tooling.
node_modules/
.cache/
